      "text": "To convert the point \\((0, -3 \\sqrt{3}, 3)\\) from rectangular coordinates to spherical coordinates, we need to use the following formulas:\n\\[\n\\rho = \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\theta = \\arctan\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\phi = \\arccos\\left(\\frac{z}{\\rho}\\right)\n\\]\n\nGiven the point \\((0, -3 \\sqrt{3}, 3)\\), we have:\n\\[\nx = 0, \\quad y = -3 \\sqrt{3}, \\quad z = 3\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate \\(\\rho\\):\n\\[\n\\rho = \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\rho = \\sqrt{0^2 + (-3 \\sqrt{3})^2 + 3^2}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\rho = \\sqrt{0 + 27 + 9}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\rho = \\sqrt{36}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\rho = 6\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(\\theta\\):\n\\[\n\\theta = \\arctan\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\theta = \\arctan\\left(\\frac{-3 \\sqrt{3}}{0}\\right)\n\\]\n\nSince the point \\((0, -3 \\sqrt{3})\\) is on the negative \\(y\\)-axis, the angle \\(\\theta\\) lies in the fourth quadrant. The arctangent of \\(\\frac{-3 \\sqrt{3}}{0}\\) is undefined, which means \\(\\theta\\) is \\(\\pi\\) radians. Therefore:\n\\[\n\\theta = \\pi\n\\]\n\nFinally, we calculate \\(\\phi\\):\n\\[\n\\phi = \\arccos\\left(\\frac{z}{\\rho}\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\phi = \\arccos\\left(\\frac{3}{6}\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\phi = \\arccos\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\phi = \\frac{\\pi}{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the spherical coordinates for the point \\((0, -3 \\sqrt{3}, 3)\\) are:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(6, \\pi, \\frac{\\pi}{3})}\n\\]",
