      "text": "To convert a point from rectangular (Cartesian) coordinates to spherical coordinates, we use the following formulas: $\\rho = \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2},$ $\\theta = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right),$ and $\\phi = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x^2 + y^2}}{z}\\right).$\n\nsince $x = 0,$ $y = -3 \\sqrt{3},$ and $z = 3,$ we have $\\rho = \\sqrt{0^2 + (-3 \\sqrt{3})^2 + 3^2} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 3 + 9} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 3 + 9} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 3 + 9} = \\sqrt{9 + 9} = \\sqrt{50} = 5 \\sqrt{2}$\n\nSince $x = 0,$ $\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right) = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{-3 \\sqrt{3}}{0}\\right)$ which is undefined.  We set $\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$ which is between 0 and $2 \\pi.$  Therefore, the spherical coordinates are $\\boxed{(5 \\sqrt{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{0^2 + (-3 \\sqrt{3})^2 + 3^2}}{3}\\right)) = (5 \\sqrt{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{50}}{3}\\right))}$\n\nEX: Converting the point $(4, -4, 4)$ to spherical coordinates.\n\nSolution: We use the same process as above, but since $\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)$ is defined, we can set $\\theta = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{-4}{4}\\right) = -\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{1}\\right) = -\\tan^{-1}(1)$ which is equal to $-\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\n\nTherefore, the spherical coordinates are $(5 \\sqrt{2}, \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{4^2 + (-4)^2}}{4}\\right), -\\frac{\\pi}{4}).$  But here, $- \\frac{\\pi}{4}$ is not between 0 and $2 \\pi,$ so it has to be changed to the equivalent positive angle.  We change the angle to $-\\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\pi = \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}$\n\nTherefore, the spherical coordinates are $\\boxed{\\left( 5 \\sqrt{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{4^2 + (-4)^2}}{4}\\right) \\right) =\\left( 5 \\sqrt{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{32}}{4}\\right) \\right) =\\left( 5 \\sqrt{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\sqrt{2}\\right) \\right).}$\n$\\rho = \\sqrt{4^2 + (-4)^2 + 4^2}$\n\n$\\theta = \\text{atan}(\\frac{-4}{4}) = {\\frac{-\\pi}{4}} Thus \\boxed{( 5\\sqrt{2}, \\tan^{-1}(\\sqrt{2}), \\pi+ \\frac{-\\pi}{4})}",
